      "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nAllow the performance CLI to accept `--cuda_graph_impl full_iteration`, matching the current Megatron-Core API. Selecting it also clears inherited per-layer graph modules, which MCore rejects for full-iteration capture.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- Add `full_iteration` to `VALID_CUDA_GRAPH_IMPLS`; the CLI help picks up the new option automatically.\n- Use the existing compatibility helper to normalize explicit full-iteration selection, while rejecting conflicting explicit scopes and preserving support for older MCore.\n- Add six regression cases for inherited settings, accepted scope forms, conflicting scopes, and the legacy fallback.\n\n# GitHub Actions CI\n\nLocal validation used an isolated Python 3.12 tooling environment without installing the GPU training stack:\n\n- Ruff 0.9.9 lint and format: passed repository-wide.\n- `uv run pre-commit run --all-files`: passed (run with `--no-project` and the isolated interpreter).\n- Existing argument parser tests: 5 passed, with `--confcutdir` excluding unrelated training fixtures.\n- Direct parser smoke check: `--cuda_graph_impl full_iteration` is accepted; existing implementation choices remain accepted.\n- CUDA graph override checks: 10 passed, including the six new cases. A temporary harness loaded the actual override function and existing test class via AST, used the real Bridge CUDA graph helpers and enums from pinned MCore `e0a4bfed`, and excluded unrelated GPU imports/fixtures. This is isolated verification, not a full training integration run.\n- Standard `TestCudaGraphOverrides` collection is blocked locally by missing `torch`; GPU training was not run.\n- Strict mypy remains non-clean: 118 errors versus 122 on the base revision. Existing untyped code and missing dependencies remain; the only added diagnostic is the new regression test's missing MCore enum import in this tooling-only environment.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\n# Before your PR is \"Ready for review\"\n\n- [x] Read and followed the contributor guidelines.\n- [x] Added necessary regression tests.\n- [x] The generated CLI help includes the new choice.\n- [ ] Run the standard override tests in the complete training environment.\n\n# Additional Information\n\nMatches the API split in NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#4292 and uses the compatibility support already introduced by #3546.\n",
